<title>FRANCE: Scor sees 165 mln ffr cap gain from Coflexip sale.</title>
<headline>Scor sees 165 mln ffr cap gain from Coflexip sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>French reinsurer Scor said on Wednesday it expected to make a 165 million franc post-tax capital gain from a sale of its 7.98 percent stake in off-share engineering company Coflexip.  </p>
<p>Scor said in a statement that brokers CDC Bourse placed the shares with French and international investors. The reinsurer did not disclose the price the shares were sold at.</p>
<p>Shares in Coflexip fell 3.6 percent to 321 francs on the back of the share placement after the market close on Tuesday, traders said earlier on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A fund manager said earlier on Wednesday the placement was done at 314 francs per share.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5542</p>
</text>
